    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5402167/chief-of-police-university-police-department": {
      "title": "Chief of Police - University Police Department",
      "description": "Chief of Police - University Police Department Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600222 Division Finance and Administration Department University Police Department Opening Date 07/08/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Chief of Police University Police Department Administrative, Full-Time Chief of Police provides administrative oversight of campus police and security, emergency management, parking, and police dispatch services to ensure a safe and secure campus environment. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance & Administration, the Chief of Police supervises a team of law enforcement, parking, and emergency personnel and ensures team collaborations with local and neighboring law enforcement personnel. The Chief of Police is responsible for creating a safe campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and guests. Primary Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership and oversight for all University police, public safety, security, emergency management, and parking operations across multiple campuses Foster a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment through community-oriented policing, crime prevention, and collaborative public safety initiatives Direct campus emergency preparedness, incident response, continuity of operations, and critical incident management, including oversight of the Emergency Operations Plan (EOP), Continuity of Operations Plan (COOP), and Incident Command System (ICS) Serve as the University's senior leader for Clery Act compliance, campus safety reporting, crime statistics, emergency notifications, risk assessments, and regulatory compliance Oversee security technology and communications systems, including surveillance, alarm, dispatch, and mass notification platforms Provide administrative leadership for parking, transportation, traffic management, ADA accessibility, and transit operations while ensuring compliance with applicable regulations Build and maintain strong partnerships with local, state, and federal law enforcement agencies, emergency management organizations, transportation partners, and community stakeholders Lead organizational planning, budgeting, policy development, accreditation efforts, performance assessment, and continuous operational improvement Recruit, develop, mentor, and evaluate department personnel while fostering a culture of accountability, professionalism, wellness, inclusion, and employee engagement Advise executive leadership on public safety, security, emergency management, and institutional risk management strategies Represent the University before governing boards, governmental agencies, community organizations, media representatives, and professional associations Champion innovative, collaborative, and data-informed approaches that support institutional resilience, student success, and the University's strategic priorities Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Criminal Justice, Public Administration, Emergency Management, Homeland Security, Business Administration, Public Safety Administration, or a closely related field required; master's degree is considered a plus Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in law enforcement, public safety, emergency management, or a related field, including supervisory, operational, and budget management responsibilities. Experience in higher education is considered a plus Must possess current Missouri POST Class A Peace Officer License or be eligible to obtain within 6 months of employment FEMA Incident Command System (ICS), National Incident Management System (NIMS), Certified Emergency Manager (CEM), Certified Public Manager (CPM), or equivalent professional certifications are considered a plus Demonstrated knowledge of local, state, and federal laws, regulations, and best practices related to law enforcement, campus safety, emergency preparedness, response, and recovery Experience developing and managing departmental budgets and financial resources Knowledge of mediation, conflict resolution, and collaborative problem-solving techniques Demonstrated ability to build effective working relationships and collaborate with internal and external stakeholders at all organizational levels Proven ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and respond effectively to sensitive or high-profile situations Strong leadership, organizational, and personnel management skills with a commitment to fostering a positive and accountable work environment Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively during emergencies and with diverse audiences Demonstrated ability to prioritize competing demands, manage multiple projects simultaneously, and perform effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions Application Process Application Deadline: The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by July 31, 2026 . To Apply : Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current Resume Names and contact information of three professional references Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5337259/data-engineer-information-technology": {
      "title": "Data Engineer - Information Technology",
      "description": "Data Engineer - Information Technology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600080 Division Finance and Administration Department Information Technology Opening Date 05/08/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Data Engineer Information Technology Full Time Primary Responsibilities Develop procedures for moving operational data into data repositories used for reporting and data analysis employing Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) tools such as SSIS and Alteryx to automate data pipeline services Implement and document needed data mappings and transformations between data sources and data repositories Incorporate error checking and alerting procedures to ensure failed procedures are caught and corrected in a timely manner Develop and support stored procedures and SQL views and queries needed for data access, cleaning and transformations. Implement methods to improve data reliability and quality Work with the Office of Institutional Research to identify existing operational data sources to support the Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW) and help develop database schemas and data models to support longitudinal data analysis Implement data access controls to support least privileged access policies for data supporting operational and strategic data uses Work with clients and the Office of Institutional Research to help develop needed reports and data dashboards. Use tools such as SSRS and Power Bi to develop and support reports and dashboards. Implement data models supporting data reporting needs Work with campus leadership to identify database platforms, data reporting and analysis tools, and data ETL systems that support campus data management needs and align with evolving technologies Required Qualifications Master’s degree in computer science or related field or a bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field along with four years of relevant experience Experience in data ETL processes and tools such as SSIS or Alteryx Experience developing queries and views in SQL Experience in data reporting using tools such as SSRS Experience with data visualization tools such as Power Bi Experience using database systems such as MS SQL Server or Snowflake Experience working in a team environment; Experience working in Higher Education is a plus Ability to effectively communicate technical procedures and concepts, both in writing and verbally, to individuals without a technical background Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process Application Deadline: The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by May 22 , 2026. To Apply : Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current Resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for at a later date Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fact Book: Institutional Research Factbook | SEMO SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5345760/director-law-enforcement-academy": {
      "title": "Director - Law Enforcement Academy",
      "description": "Director - Law Enforcement Academy Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600105-01 Division Academic Affairs Department Criminal Justice, Social Work and Sociology Opening Date 09/14/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Law Enforcement Academy Department of Criminal Justice, Social Work, and Sociology Full Time Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO) invites applications for a highly qualified, results-oriented, professional to serve as Law Enforcement Academy Director. The Academy operates under the Department of Criminal Justice, Social Work, and Sociology as a Missouri POST Commission authorized Training Center to provide initial training to new recruits, required annual training to officers, and specialized training to individual units and newly promoted officers. The Director is responsible for overseeing, managing, and supporting the design, implementation, management, and evaluation of all training programs for the Academy. The Director will facilitate professional development and continuing education and ensure all personnel are highly qualified and well equipped to perform their duties in a constitutional and impartial manner. The ideal candidate will be forward-thinking, strategic, and innovative, including leveraging information technology to help achieve continuous improvement. The Director will evaluate Academy faculty, develop new training curricula and lesson plans, and provide guidance on methods and practices of teaching to Academy staff and adjunct instructors. The Director will ensure the academic integrity of the Academy and the training programs offered, promote innovative teaching techniques, and manage partnerships with local law enforcement agencies. Primary Responsibilities Serve as the POST-authorized Training Center Director and act under the Department Chairperson in that role. Manage daily operations of training and standards for the Academy, including scheduling, logistics, and resource management. Supervise training staff, adjunct instructors, and support personnel. Maintain records for audit, accreditation, and funding purposes. Ensure effective and efficient use of training budgets and personnel allocations. Prepare reports, training metrics, and performance evaluations. Lead strategic initiatives to evolve academy training methods. Develop and maintain Continuing Law Enforcement Education (CLEE) certified curriculum and annual training calendar. Coordinate advanced training opportunities for regional law enforcement personnel. Ensure curriculum development, instructional quality, and regulatory compliance for the Law Enforcement Academy. Collaborate with academic partners to integrate Academy training with higher education pathways. Actively participate in law enforcement networks and advisory boards. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in criminal justice, public administration, or related field; Master’s degree a plus. (Degree must be from a regionally accredited college or university.) Missouri POST Class A Peace Officer License or ability to obtain within 6 months. Missouri POST Generalist Instructor Certification or ability to obtain within 6 months. Minimum of 12 years of progressive law enforcement experience, including advanced leadership training and supervisory duties. Demonstrated knowledge of law enforcement training standards, principles, and adult education techniques. Demonstrated knowledge and innovative approaches to modern law enforcement principles, techniques, and practices. Demonstrated ability to foster collaboration with internal and external constituents. Ability to work evenings or weekends as needed. Ability to travel regionally for training coordination and academy promotion. Excellent interpersonal, presentation, and oral and written communication skills. Application Process Application Deadline: The review of applications will begin immediately. Required Information: To apply, submit the following items online by clicking on the Apply button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing required position qualifications Current resume Copies of POST Licenses and Certificates Unofficial copies of transcripts (official transcripts are required when an offer of employment is accepted) Names and contact information of three professional references Additional Information Departmental Information: The Department of Criminal Justice, Social Work, and Sociology houses numerous degree programs and the Southeast Law Enforcement Academy. Academic offerings include undergraduate degree programs (BS) in Criminal Justice and Social Work; undergraduate minors in Criminology & Criminal Justice, Social Work, and Sociology; an undergraduate certificate program in Law Enforcement; and a graduate degree (MS) in Criminal Justice. Several programs are available fully online, and the department strongly supports Prior Learning Credit (PLC) and experiential learning. More information regarding the Department of Criminal Justice, Social Work, and Sociology can be found at https://semo.edu/cjsws/ . The Social Work Program is CSWE Accredited, and the Law Enforcement Academy is a Missouri POST Commission Licensed Training Center. About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts | SEMO Strategic Action Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5414290/director-of-corporate-partnerships-business-development-athletics": {
      "title": "Director of Corporate Partnerships & Business Development - Athletics",
      "description": "Director of Corporate Partnerships & Business Development - Athletics Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600238 Division Athletics Department Athletics Opening Date 07/17/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director of Corporate Partnerships & Business Development Department of Athletics Position Summary Southeast Missouri State University is seeking a motivated and results-oriented Director of Corporate Partnerships & Business Development to grow business-to-business revenue opportunities for SEMO Athletics. Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for External Operations with a dual-reporting relationship to University Advancement, this position is responsible for generating revenue through corporate sponsorships, business-focused ticket sales, corporate outings, Alumni Magazine advertising, sponsorship inventory management, and corporate partnership execution. The successful candidate will be a proactive seller, strong relationship builder, creative problem solver, and detail-oriented professional who creates value for corporate partners while advancing sustainable revenue growth for SEMO Athletics. Primary Responsibilities Identify, prospect, cultivate, pitch, negotiate, and secure corporate sponsorships, advertising opportunities, corporate ticket packages, and other business-to-business revenue opportunities Develop and manage relationships with corporate partners to support satisfaction, retention, renewals and revenue growth Sell advertising in the University’s Alumni Magazine, as standalone opportunities or as part of integrated corporate partnership packages Manage SEMO Athletics sponsorship and advertising inventory, including availability, pricing, category exclusivity, contracts, renewals, fulfillment requirements, and partner activation needs Coordinate sponsorship activation and fulfillment in collaboration with athletics department and campus partners to ensure corporate partnership agreements are executed accurately, professionally, and on schedule Support Name, Image, and Likeness (NIL) and revenue sharing initiatives by identifying business opportunities, managing available NIL-related inventory or concepts, supporting student-athlete fulfillment, and coordinating with appropriate Athletics, University, and compliance staff Support fundraising events, home athletic events, and other external engagement revenue-generating initiatives Utilize Raiser’s Edge NXT, Paciolan/PacFund, and other systems to manage prospects, document sales activity and partner communication, monitor inventory, forecast revenue and measure performance Represent SEMO Athletics at home athletic events, select away athletic events, fundraising and donor functions, community and University events, and regional engagement opportunities, including evenings, weekends, and occasional travel Ensure all revenue-generation and activation activities are conducted in accordance with University policies, NCAA rules, conference regulations, state laws, and contractual obligations Maintain a valid driver's license Perform other duties as assigned in support of SEMO Athletics and University Advancement priorities Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution Two or more years of experience in sales, business development, sports marketing, athletics external operations, fundraising, or another relationship-based sales or business development field Knowledge of intercollegiate athletics and the business of sports marketing and sponsorships Demonstrated ability to prospect, build relationships, present opportunities, negotiate agreements, close sales, and provide follow-up service Demonstrated ability to manage client relationships, deliver excellent customer service, and support retention efforts Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including proposal development, presentations, correspondence, and reporting Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, initiative, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment Ability to develop creative sponsorship, advertising, ticket sales, and revenue-generating opportunities Ability to work collaboratively with a variety of audiences, including Athletics and University leadership, coaches, staff, donors, alumni, volunteers, business partners, and campus colleagues Ability to use CRM systems, ticketing platforms, Microsoft Office, presentation software, or similar technology Ability to work frequent evenings and weekends, and travel occasionally as required Commitment to NCAA rules compliance, University policies, confidentiality, and ethical standards Possess a valid driver’s license Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by July 31, 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You must submit the following for your application materials to be complete. Letter of interest addressing all position qualifications Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information Department Website: Department of Athletics About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5375651/director-application-services-information-technology": {
      "title": "Director, Application Services - Information Technology",
      "description": "Director, Application Services - Information Technology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600125 Division Finance and Administration Department Information Technology Opening Date 06/12/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Application Services Information Technology Full Time Primary Responsibilities Provide day-to-day leadership, guidance, and performance management for a team of programmer/analysts and data engineers supporting university applications, business systems and data integration needs Mentor staff in problem analysis, programming best practices, data protection/compliance, and office procedures Set priorities and assign and schedule work to ensure projects, upgrades, problems resolutions, and needed integrations are accomplished Coordinate project work and establish realistic goals and expectations Work with staff as needed to support ERP systems and resolve problems Coordinate with functional offices (Admissions, Finance, HR, Registrar, etc.) to ensure solutions meet business requirements Chair the Business Systems Management Committee and help set goals, timelines, and direction for system development and support Oversee adherence to development methodologies, documentation standards, and change-management processes Set standards for application and database development Work with staff to track and document system development and support for business continuity Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in computer science or information technology Five years' experience working in a team environment developing and supporting database driven software applications; experience in Banner a plus Demonstrated competency in one or more programming languages; experience developing in Visual Studio in Visual C a plus Experience developing queries and views in SQL Experience in data reporting; experience using SSRS is a plus Experience using database systems such as MS SQL Server Experience working in a team environment; experience working in higher education is a plus Supervisory experience Ability to communicate technical procedures and concepts, both in writing and verbally to individuals without a technical background Demonstrated experience and understanding of quality customer service Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by July 5 , 2026 . The position will remain open until filled To Apply : Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current Resume Names and contact information of three professional references Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
