    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5472359/director-center-for-advanced-professional-studies-caps-economic-and-workforc": {
      "title": "Director, Center for Advanced Professional Studies (CAPS) - Economic and Workforce Development",
      "description": "Director, Center for Advanced Professional Studies (CAPS) - Economic and Workforce Development Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600297 Division President Department Office of Economic and Workforce Development Opening Date 09/03/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Center for Advanced Professional Studies (CAPS) Division of Economic and Workforce Development Full Time Position Summary The Director of the Center for Advanced Professional Studies (CAPS) provides leadership and oversight for Southeast Missouri State University's CAPS program. This position develops and maintains partnerships with K-12 school districts, business and industry leaders, and community stakeholders to create career-focused learning experiences for high school students. The Director oversees program planning, operations, curriculum alignment, student recruitment, and stakeholder engagement to ensure high-quality educational opportunities. As the program's lead administrator, the Director supports program growth, strengthens workforce partnerships, and helps students prepare for college, careers, and lifelong success while advancing regional workforce and economic development goals. Primary Responsibilities Collaborate with SEMO leadership and local/regional businesses to recruit, develop, retain, and engage industry partners that support student learning through internships, project-based experiences, and other workforce engagement opportunities Recruit, develop, support, and provide professional development opportunities for CAPS instructors, guest speakers/instructors, and staff, to ensure a high-quality learning experience for students Build and maintain productive relationships with high school administrators and expand partnerships with high schools through origination and management of Memorandums of Understanding (MOUs) Partner closely with SEMO departments, including student financial services, marketing and communications, facilities management, and IT, to ensure seamless program operations Work collaboratively with counselors, students, and families to ensure CAPS coursework aligns with student interests, academic goals, graduation requirements, and schedules Work with SEMO leadership to develop and implement internal and external marketing and communications strategies that increase program visibility and impact Oversee curriculum development, implementation, evaluation, and record keeping processes, using multiple forms of assessment data to enhance program quality, support student success, and explore future program offerings Monitor student attendance, academic progress, and behavior; collaborate with schools, families, instructors, and mentors to develop individualized intervention and success plans; and serve as the primary point of contact for high school personnel regarding student concerns Oversee the application, selection, and enrollment processes for prospective CAPS students, developing streamlined procedures that align with participating school districts Coordinate and manage recruitment and outreach activities, including tours, open houses, orientation events, and career fairs Provide strategic leadership and oversight for all CAPS program operations Support student future success by coordinating business partner recommendations, references, and testimonials that strengthen admissions and scholarship opportunities Promote a culture of professionalism by upholding CAPS expectations related to conduct, workplace readiness, attendance, and professional appearance Oversee student fee processes and collections while ensuring sound fiscal stewardship and operational efficiency Required Qualifications Master’s degree with examples of experience in curriculum and/or workforce development 5+ years of progressively responsible experience, demonstrating education, education leadership, counseling, career development and/or related experience within a K-12 or Higher Education setting Strong leadership and administrative skills including planning, budgeting, and resource management Demonstrated experience in data collection, analysis, and report writing Demonstrated successful communication and stakeholder engagement skills to build partnerships and lead collaborative initiatives Experience delivering engaging presentations to internal and external audiences Excellent written and verbal communication skills Excellent problem-solving abilities Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by September 17, 2026. The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You will need to submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete. Cover letter Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5439541/director-destination-semo-economic-and-workforce-development": {
      "title": "Director, Destination SEMO - Economic and Workforce Development",
      "description": "Director, Destination SEMO - Economic and Workforce Development Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600266 Division President Department Office of Economic and Workforce Development Opening Date 08/06/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Destination SEMO Division of Economic and Workforce Development Full-Time Position Summary The Director of Destination SEMO provides leadership for a university-wide engagement initiative designed to position Southeast Missouri State University as a regional destination for learning, culture, athletics, events, workforce development, and community engagement. The Director functions as the university's destination strategist, coordinating existing campus resources, experiences, partnerships, and visitor engagement efforts into a unified Destination SEMO framework. The position serves as a connector across corporate, academic, administrative, cultural, athletic, and community-based units to create exceptional experiences that strengthen recruitment, alumni engagement, economic impact, community relationships, lifelong learning participation, and institutional reputation. Primary Responsibilities Develop the Destination SEMO vision and operational plan, based on the Fearlessly Forward strategic plan Implement programs, and initiatives that invite corporate and private organizations/associations on-to campus through space rental and specialty events Position SEMO as a leading regional destination for education, culture, athletics, conferences, workforce development, and community engagement Analyze trends, recommend strategies, and market opportunities for growth and revenue generation. Establish goals, priorities, and performance measures aligned with university objectives Collaborate with Marketing and Communications to promote SEMO as a place to visit, experience, learn, and connect Develop partnership and sales opportunities that increase visibility, attendance, and regional impact Serve as the university advocate for visitor engagement and destination development initiatives Collaborate with campus and community partners to develop, integrate, package, and promote academic, cultural, athletic, recreational, and community experiences that encourage additional engagement Leverage programs, events, conferences, camps, and themed experiences to create marketable destination offerings that strengthen SEMO's appeal and regional impact Lead and coordinate a seamless visitor experience across campus by collaborating with university departments to enhance visitor services, engagement programs, wayfinding, communications, and support resources Ensure consistency of messaging across visitor-focused programs and experiences Develop and maintain systems to measure visitor engagement, attendance, participation, satisfaction, and economic impact, prepare reports for university leadership Required Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, Public Administration, Tourism Management, Economic Development, Marketing, Communications, or a related field Minimum five years of progressively responsible leadership experience in one or more of the following areas: Higher Education, economic development, destination management, tourism, community engagement, workforce development Experience in destination marketing, tourism development, visitor experience management, or community engagement; experience working in a college or university environment is a plus Demonstrated success in building partnerships and leading collaborative initiatives Strong project management, communication (verbal and written), and organizational skills Demonstrated ability to measure outcomes and assess economic impact Experience leading cross-functional teams and strategic initiatives Experience actively engaging potential clients and customers in a sales capacity Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain professional relationships within and external to the organization Experience handling sensitive and confidential information Demonstrated experience managing budgets and revenue sources Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by August 20, 2026. The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You will need to submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete. Cover letter Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fact Book SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5507289/director-redhawks-discover-enrollment-strategy": {
      "title": "Director, Redhawks Discover - Enrollment Strategy",
      "description": "Director, Redhawks Discover - Enrollment Strategy Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600342 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Enrollment Management and Student Success Opening Date 10/06/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Redhawks Discover Enrollment Strategy Full Time/Term Southeast Missouri State University seeks a professional to lead the University’s Redhawks Discover program. This four semester non-degree seeking post-secondary comprehensive transition program (CTP) is for young adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities. The mission of the program is to offer opportunities for students to develop the skills to transition to independent living and obtain competitive employment that aligns with their individual goals and abilities. The program is built around four pillars: academics, independent living, social development, and employment. Upon completion of the program students will be issued a certificate of Career Readiness. Primary Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership for program planning, launch, growth, and sustainability, including oversight of operations, budget, staffing, policies, and assessment Develop, implement, and evaluate policies addressing student participation, safety, confidentiality, conduct, and emergency response Ensure compliance with university requirements, grant funding agreements, applicable accreditation standards, and federal Comprehensive Transition Program requirements Oversee data collection, analysis, and reporting on recruitment, enrollment, retention, completion, student progress, and employment outcomes. Use findings and stakeholder feedback to guide planning, recruitment, resource allocation, and continuous improvement Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate staff, student employees, peer mentors, and other personnel; coordinate faculty participation Lead the advisory board, including member recruitment, engagement, meetings, and contributions to program planning and evaluation Coordinate student recruitment, admissions, onboarding, transition, and orientation in collaboration with university offices, students, and families Oversee individualized, person-centered learning plans and approve weekly student schedules. Coordinate academic, employment, independent living, and social supports through appropriate personnel Provide ongoing education for students and families on independence, healthy boundaries, self-advocacy, autonomy, and changing roles during college Train and support university faculty and staff to promote student inclusion and success across campus Build campus, community, agency, and employer partnerships supporting internships, employment, extracurricular involvement, community engagement, and independent living. Collaborate with SEMO Career Services, state workforce development job centers, and Missouri Vocational Rehabilitation to expand employment preparation and placement Maintain regular communication with students, families, personnel, university offices, community partners, employers, funders, and advisory board members Respond to urgent student or program situations under established emergency procedures, including assigned after-hours responsibilities Participate in professional development related to inclusive higher education, postsecondary transition, disability services, employment, and evidence-based practices; perform other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in special education, social work, rehabilitation, counseling, family science, human development, higher education, or another closely related field Professional experience working with individuals with intellectual, developmental, or other disabilities Leadership and staff management experience Demonstrated experience managing budgets and revenue sources Strong knowledge of federal Comprehensive Transition Program requirements and recognized standards in inclusive higher education Excellent communication and collaboration skills Strong computer and technical skills Proficiency with student information systems for data collection, assessment, reporting, and continuous program improvement Detail-oriented with strong organizational and problem-solving abilities Exercises sound judgment Demonstrated experience and understanding of person-centered planning and outcomes Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by October 20, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button on the top of the page. You must submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete: • Letter of interest addressing all required position qualifications • Resume • Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5457636/director-workforce-training-economic-and-workforce-development": {
      "title": "Director, Workforce Training - Economic and Workforce Development",
      "description": "Director, Workforce Training - Economic and Workforce Development Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600291 Division President Department Office of Economic and Workforce Development Opening Date 08/21/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Director, Workforce Training Division of Economic and Workforce Development Full Time The Director of Workforce Training provides strategic leadership, development, implementation, and evaluation of workforce training programs that support regional economic growth and meet employer talent needs. The position oversees workforce training operations, partnerships, budgets, grants, and program outcomes. Primary Responsibilities Develop and execute a workforce training strategy aligned with regional workforce and economic development priorities, utilizing labor market intelligence and employer feedback to identify skill needs and talent development opportunities Lead the planning, development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of workforce training programs, and customized training solutions, that address employer demand and support workforce advancement Establish and monitor department goals, key performance indicators, and outcome measures to assess program effectiveness, ensure continuous improvement, and demonstrate workforce and economic impact Cultivate and maintain strategic partnerships with employers, industry associations, chambers of commerce, workforce agencies, educational institutions, government entities, and economic development organizations to advance workforce development initiatives and respond to regional talent needs Serve as the primary liaison for workforce training partnerships, contracts, and employer engagement efforts, and assist in the development of work-based learning opportunities Identify, pursue, secure, and administer grants and other funding resources that support workforce training initiatives, ensuring compliance with funding requirements, budget expectations, and reporting obligations Recruit, supervise, and evaluate workforce training temporary staff and students while fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, accountability, and customer service Ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, local, accreditation, and organizational requirements, maintaining accurate program records, performance data, and documentation Prepare and present reports, analyses, presentations, and recommendations for leadership, funding agencies, governing bodies, and external stakeholders regarding program performance, workforce outcomes, and strategic initiatives Represent the organization at community, industry, workforce, and economic development meetings, conferences, advisory boards, and public events to promote workforce training programs and strengthen regional partnerships Perform other related duties as assigned in support of workforce development, talent pipeline expansion, and organizational objectives Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree with equivalent experience in training, workforce development or another related field Minimum seven years of progressively responsible experience, demonstrating education, counseling, career development and/or related experience Strong leadership and administrative skills including planning, budgeting, and resource management Experience managing and/or using computerized data information systems Demonstrated experience in data collection, analysis, and report writing Experience delivering engaging presentations to internal and external audiences Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Excellent problem-solving abilities Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Available to work evenings and weekends Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by September 4, 2026. The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You will need to submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete. Cover letter Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Action Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
