      "description": "Dispatcher - University Police Department Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600079-01 Division Finance and Administration Department University Police Department Opening Date 09/15/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary DISPATCHER University Police Department Full time Primary Responsibilities Monitors, receives and directs routine and emergency telephone calls to the department, performing a variety of duties of a public service agency Monitors, receives and transmits routine and emergency radio transmissions to fulfill requests for services and support of officers on duty Manages software-based multi-channel radio communications, Missouri Uniform Law Enforcement System (MULES), and input data into a software- based dispatch and records management system Enters and retrieves confidential computer records and disseminates information to appropriate personnel Monitors fire alarms, security cameras, and environmental alarms Performs various support duties related to dispatch functions, including record keeping, typing, filing, and logs Operates mass notification systems such as Regroup and Alertus and deploys the indoor/outdoor warning system (storm sirens) Provides logistical support to parking services, transit services, and other university service providers Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED MULES certified or eligible for MULES certification within 6-months of employment Ability to effectively operate dispatch technology; Experience in police dispatching a plus Knowledge of MS Office Excellent interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills Ability to work all shifts, specifically the midnight shift, but also including day and evening shifts, weekends, Holidays, and during academic breaks Ability to work independently with minimal supervision Demonstrated problem solving abilities Demonstrated experience with and understanding of customer service Required 