    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5439385/engineering-pathway-coordinator-admissions-and-new-student-programs": {
      "title": "Engineering Pathway Coordinator - Admissions and New Student Programs",
      "description": "Engineering Pathway Coordinator - Admissions and New Student Programs Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600273 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Admissions and New Student Programs Opening Date 08/06/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Engineering Pathway Coordinator Office of Admissions and New Student Programs Full- Time Position Summary The Engineering Pathway Coordinator serves as the primary recruitment, enrollment, and student success professional for Southeast Missouri State University's engineering partnership with Missouri University of Science and Technology (Missouri S&T). This position recruits prospective students, guides them through the admissions process, provides individualized pathway planning and academic support, and builds relationships that promote student persistence and successful transfer to Missouri S&T. The Coordinator combines the relationship-building and territory management responsibilities of an admissions counselor with the advising, coaching, and student success functions of a transfer coordinator. The position serves as the primary point of contact for students and families from initial inquiry through transition to Missouri S&T. The successful candidate will be a self-motivated, results-oriented, energetic professional who can succeed working independently. They will be a member of the University’s admissions and new student programs team – a team that is student-focused and committed to offering personal support for every student to persist in college and complete their degree. This role is integral to the University’s enrollment management efforts and responsible for developing new student enrollment to meet institutional goals. Primary Responsibilities Recruitment and Enrollment Management Recruit prospective students interested in engineering pathway opportunities Manage assigned recruitment territories and recruitment initiatives Conduct individual outreach through phone, email, text messaging, video conferencing, and in-person meetings Build relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, STEM educators, and community partners Represent the University at college fairs, recruitment events, high school visits, and engineering-focused programs Coordinate and participate in on-campus recruitment and yield events Student Advising and Success Coaching Serve as the primary point of contact for students enrolled in the engineering pathway program Assist students in understanding pathway requirements, academic expectations, and transfer milestones Provide developmental advising and success coaching focused on persistence, engagement, and academic achievement Monitor student progress and proactively intervene when challenges arise Connect students with academic support, financial aid, career development, tutoring, and other campus resources Support students and families throughout the transition to Missouri S&T Partnership Coordination Collaborate with SEMO faculty, advisors, admissions staff, and student support teams Maintain strong working relationships with Missouri S&T admissions, advising, and engineering representatives Coordinate communication and information sharing between partner institutions Assist with pathway events, campus visits, orientation activities, and student engagement initiatives Data Management and Reporting Maintain accurate student records in CRM, student information, retention, and advising systems Track recruitment activities, enrollment outcomes, retention metrics, and transfer success indicators Analyze data and provide recommendations to improve recruitment, enrollment, retention, and student success outcomes Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree Demonstrated experience in recruitment, admissions, advising, student services, sales, customer service, or related fields Proficient in the use of technology tools used to manage information, including the Microsoft Office Suite Excellent interpersonal, presentation, verbal, and written communication skills Strong problem-solving, organizational, and time-management skills Ability to build relationships with students, families, faculty, counselors, and external partners Committed to delivering exceptional customer service Excels working independently with minimal supervision Ability to work in a collaborative environment and exercise sound judgment Ability to travel extensively, with or without accommodation, and work alternate schedules, including evenings and weekends Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds of publications and display materials, with or without accommodation Possess and maintain a valid state driver's license Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by August 20, 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You will need to submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete. Letter of interest addressing the required qualifications Current resume Names and contact information for three professional references may be asked at a a later date, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fact Book SEMO Strategic Action Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
