    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5511002/horticulturist-facilities-management": {
      "title": "Horticulturist - Facilities Management",
      "description": "Horticulturist - Facilities Management Salary See Position Description Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600340 Division Finance and Administration Department Facilities Management Opening Date 10/08/2026 Closing Date 10/23/2026 11:59 PM Central Description Benefits Position Summary Horticulturist Facilities Management Full Time Starting Wage : $23.37 per hour Primary Responsibilities Select, order and track landscaping plant materials and supplies Oversee and coordinate small project teams during spring/fall plantings Maintain University landscape beds and outdoor planters Work with Grounds Supervisor and Grounds lead to create a master plan of plantings for all Main and River Campus beds and planters Prepare all beds and planters prior to spring/fall planting Maintain all beds and planters throughout the season including watering, applying plant protection and nutrition products, weeding, and mulching Dispose of plant material and prepare beds at end of the growing season Mowing and trimming University lawns as directed Operate mowers and string trimmers to maintain University grounds Help with any other related project work on university grounds including campus irrigation, and athletic fields Clean the equipment and maintenance areas; return all equipment to the designated location at the maintenance facility Snow and ice removal as necessary Maintain driver’s license Required Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Horticulture or Agriculture related field and/or minimum one year of industry work experience Demonstrated work history reflecting reliability and dependability Possess a valid driver’s license Ability to work in inclement weather, including emergencies and snow removal, and live within 30 minutes travel time from the University Knowledge of proper planting, cultivating, and caring for plants Knowledge of soil composition and the use of soil amendments Knowledge of proper pruning techniques for plants, shrubs, and trees Demonstrated ability to use hand-held tools and grounds equipment Demonstrated ability to operate trucks and tractors of various sizes and weights in loading hauling and unloading various equipment and supplies Possess MO Pesticide License or must obtain within 90 days of hire Ability to stoop, bend, stand, walk, kneel or crouch frequently and for extended periods of time Ability to occasionally lift, carry and/or drag up to 50 pounds Ability to Follow Written and Verbal Instructions and Perform Duties with Minimal Supervision Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by October 23, 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page and complete every section of the online application including providing three professional references. Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
