    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5460360/occupational-therapist-autism-center-for-diagnosis-and-treatment": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist - Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment",
      "description": "Occupational Therapist - Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600292 Division Academic Affairs Department Autism Center Opening Date 08/25/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Occupational Therapist Southeast Missouri State University Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment Full Time The Autism Center is dedicated to helping children and families affected by autism reach their full potential through compassionate, family-centered, and evidence-based services. As a leading multidisciplinary provider in Southeast Missouri, we deliver individualized assessment and treatment services while fostering inclusion, collaboration, and advocacy. Our team is committed to improving access to quality care, empowering families with the support and resources they need, and helping every child thrive at home, in school, and in the community. Primary Responsibilities: Conduct thorough occupational therapy evaluations for clients with autism spectrum disorder, including sensory processing, motor skills, activities of daily living, feeding skills, and support for AAC evaluations, to determine functional strengths, needs, and recommendations for intervention Develop individualized treatment plans based on assessment findings, client goals, and family priorities Implement evidence-based occupational therapy interventions to address sensory integration, fine and gross motor skills, and self-regulation Utilize a variety of therapeutic techniques, adaptive equipment, and sensory tools to optimize client outcomes Collaborate with families and caregivers to educate them about the goals of therapy, home exercise programs, and strategies for supporting skill development in daily routines Maintain accurate and timely documentation of client assessments, treatment sessions, daily notes, and discharge summaries Prepare written reports for stakeholders and insurance payors and participate in multidisciplinary team meetings to review client progress and adjust treatment plans as needed Stay current with advances in occupational therapy practice, particularly as they relate to autism Collaborate effectively with speech-language pathologists, behavior analysts, psychologists, educators, and other professionals to ensure coordinated care and integrated treatment approaches Provide 25-35 billable client contact hours per week Required Qualifications Master’s degree in occupational therapy from an accredited program Current MO state licensure or eligibility for licensure as an Occupational Therapist within 3 months of hire Current CPR or BLS certification or the ability to obtain certification upon hire Minimum of two years of professional experience working with individuals with developmental delays or developmental disabilities; Experience working with individuals with autism spectrum disorder is a plus Strong verbal, interpersonal and written communication skills, with the ability to build rapport with clients and their families Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team Demonstrated understanding and strong commitment to customer service Application Process Application Deadline: The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by September 9, 2026. To Apply : Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current Resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for at a later date Copy of certification and license Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5459740/outreach-and-retention-specialist-student-financial-services": {
      "title": "Outreach and Retention Specialist - Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Outreach and Retention Specialist - Student Financial Services Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600295 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Student Financial Services Opening Date 08/25/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Outreach and Retention Specialist Student Financial Services Full-Time Southeast Missouri State University is seeking an Outreach and Retention Specialist to join the Student Financial Services team. This position plays an important role in helping prospective and current students understand and navigate the financial aid process while supporting enrollment and student retention efforts. The Outreach and Retention Specialist serves as a primary point of contact for incoming and first-year students and their families regarding financial aid opportunities. The position provides individualized financial aid counseling, supports scholarship processing, participates in outreach and recruitment activities, and proactively works with students to identify and address financial barriers that may affect their ability to enroll and persist at Southeast. This position is ideal for an individual who enjoys working directly with students and families, explaining complex information in an understandable way, building relationships, and collaborating with campus partners to help students achieve their educational goals. Primary Responsibilities Serve as a primary financial aid resource for incoming, first-year, and prospective students and their families Provide individualized counseling and guidance regarding federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid opportunities, including grants, scholarships, loans, and work-study Explain financial aid eligibility requirements, application procedures, deadlines, and award information to students and families Develop and maintain knowledge of federal Title IV regulations, financial aid methodology, application requirements, and financial aid packaging procedures Lead policy research, implementation, documentation, and training related to processes affecting incoming and first-year students Assist with the review and processing of financial aid applications and ensure awards are administered accurately and in accordance with applicable regulations and University policies Respond to inquiries related to scholarships Maintain proactive communication with incoming and first-year students and identify potential financial or administrative barriers that could affect enrollment or retention Work collaboratively with campus departments and other University partners to develop solutions to student concerns and connect students with appropriate resources Participate in student retention initiatives and contribute to strategies designed to support student persistence Represent Student Financial Services at student orientations, Paying for College Nights, FAFSA completion events, recruitment activities, high school visits, community events, and other outreach programs Present financial aid information to students, families, schools, community organizations, and other groups Participate in the development, implementation, documentation, and training of departmental procedures Stay current with changes in federal, state, and institutional financial aid policies and communicate relevant changes to appropriate staff and stakeholders Provide excellent customer service through in-person, telephone, email, and other communication channels Maintain confidentiality and protect sensitive student information in accordance with FERPA and University policies Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution Experience in financial aid, higher education, student services, admissions, advising, or a customer service related field; two or more years of experience working in student financial aid or a related higher education environment is a plus Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and establish trust relationships with students, families, and diverse audiences Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Strong problem-solving and critical-thinking skills Ability to interpret and apply federal, state, and institutional policies and regulations by explaining complex information in a clear and understandable manner Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively as a team and independently Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills Demonstrated attention to accuracy and detail while managing multiple priorities and meeting established deadlines Demonstrated commitment to confidentiality and sensitive information Ability to work effectively in a high-volume environment Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by September 8, 2026. The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Complete the application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You will need to submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete. Cover letter Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/4928920/police-officer-university-police-department": {
      "title": "Police Officer - University Police Department",
      "description": "Police Officer - University Police Department Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500057 Division Finance and Administration Opening Date 07/29/2025 Description Benefits Position Summary Police Officer University Police Full Time Primary Responsibilities Protects and serves the students, visitors, faculty, and staff of the Southeast Missouri State University campus Patrols and protects the properties, buildings and grounds of campus Investigates crimes for presentation to municipal and county attorneys for criminal prosecutions Responds to requests for service and campus emergencies Enforces student Code of Conduct and makes referrals to the Office of Student Conduct Conducts patrols and makes routine security checks of campus buildings Performs protective duties to provide police services in assigned areas of campus Provides safety and crime prevention education for the campus community Maintains a valid driver license Maintains Post certification Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED; college coursework or degree a plus Must be Missouri POST certified or have completed an approved academy training program and become Missouri POST certified by first day of employment Must possess a valid Missouri driver license Must be available to work any hours, rotating shifts, days, nights, weekends and holidays; subject to call in as needed Excellent verbal and written communication skills Excellent problem-solving abilities and organizational skills Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service and community policing philosophy Demonstrated sound judgement in handling sensitive situations with tact, discretion and confidentiality Required Background Check: Must successfully pass all Assessments, Pre-Employment Testing, and Post-Offer Testing which at a minimum will include a criminal background check, polygraph exam and drug testing. Must be 21 years of age, a United States citizen, with no felony convictions of moral turpitude, or misdemeanor domestic violence convictions. Failure to pass will result in the employment offer being revoked. Application Process To Apply: Click on the APPLY button at the top of the page and complete every section of the online application. A letter of interest addressing all position qualifications and a current resume is required. The review of applications will begin immediately. Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/4988705/police-officer-cadet-university-police-department": {
      "title": "Police Officer, Cadet - University Police Department",
      "description": "Police Officer, Cadet - University Police Department Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500057-01 Division Finance and Administration Department University Police Department Opening Date 06/27/2025 Description Benefits Position Summary Police Officer - Cadet Department of Public Safety and Transit Full Time A cadet police officer is a paid trainee position within the Department of Public Safety at Southeast Missouri State University, designed to prepare individuals for a career in law enforcement. The successful candidate must attend and complete the SEMO Law Enforcement Academy program and in accordance with the Missouri Peace Officers Standard and Training Act of 1979 graduate with a Class A License by the Missouri Department of Public Safety. Primary Responsibilities Serve as first responder to calls for service from students, faculty, staff and visitors concerning criminal or civil complaints, maintenance problems, safety situations, parking, alarms sounding, etc Assist in ensuring the safety and protection of students, employees and visitors on campus; provide transportation as appropriate Patrol all properties, buildings, and grounds of the campus both in a vehicle and on foot, parking lots and roadways, residence halls and enforce all regulations concerning alcohol, noise and visitation Enforce the rules and regulations of Southeast Missouri State University; Enforce city, state, and federal laws Enforce regulations pertaining to security, safety and proper usage of university property, and be alert for hazards on the premises which could endanger the safety of persons on campus Lock and unlock all doors, examine windows, lights and gates to ensure that they are secure Permit authorized persons to enter campus and observe departing individuals in order to prevent theft of university property Report all irregularities, fire hazards, leaks, etc. and make notifications to appropriate individuals for response Participate in fire drills and traffic and parking control Maintain training as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) as it relates to the Clery Act Maintain valid drivers license Required Qualifications Must have high school diploma or GED Possess a valid Missouri operator’s license Willingness to attend SEMO Regional Law Enforcement Academy Available to work flexible hours consisting of rotating shifts, to include days, evenings, midnights, weekends and holidays Excellent verbal and written communication skills Excellent problem-solving abilities Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Demonstrated sound judgement in Handling sensitive situations with tact, discretion and confidentiality Required Background Check: Must successfully pass all Assessments, Pre-Employment Testing, and Post-Offer Testing which at a minimum will include a criminal background check, polygraph exam and drug testing. Must be 21 years of age, a United States citizen, with no felony convictions of moral turpitude, or misdemeanor domestic violence convictions. Failure to pass will result in the employment offer being revoked. Application Process To Apply: Click on the APPLY button at the top of the page and complete every section of the online application. A letter of interest addressing all position qualifications and a current resume is required. The review of applications will begin immediately. Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5487341/provost-and-vice-president-for-academic-affairs": {
      "title": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600325 Division Academic Affairs Department Provost Opening Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Summary Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Southeast Missouri State University, a dynamic and competitive regional public comprehensive institution located in Cape Girardeau, Missouri, invites nominations and applications for the position of Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs (“Provost”). The Provost is the chief academic officer of the University, providing executive leadership, direction, and evaluation for the institution’s academic enterprise. Role and Responsibilities: Reporting to the University President, the Provost oversees colleges, schools, offices, and operations including: Holland College of Arts and Media; Harrison College of Business and Computing; College of Education, Health, and Human Studies; College of Humanities and Social Sciences; College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics; Graduate Studies; Kent Library; Center for Teaching and Learning; Jane Stephens Honors Program; Institutional Research; Regional campuses; Academic Advising; Center for Writing Excellence and Learning Assistance Programs; and Program review, approval, and accreditation. Ensure academic staff have active and expanding relationships with external stakeholders, including but not limited to partnerships with government, industry, regional education institutions, and robust engagement with University Advancement. Develop and implement a strategic academic vision, authorize faculty hiring, recommend promotion and tenure decisions to the University President, facilitate and evaluate major academic initiatives, oversee academic budgets, oversee academic councils and committees, and ensure high academic quality and outcomes. Provide executive leadership and institutional support for regional and specialized accreditation, academic compliance, assessment, and continuous improvement. Serve as the University President’s first delegate, ensuring the continuity and quality of ongoing operations in his absence. Partner with members of the President’s Cabinet to develop programs and initiatives that enhance student recruitment, retention, and success, and promote the overall mission, vision, and strategic plan for the university. Remain competent and current through self-directed professional reading, development opportunities, and other training. Contribute to the overall success of the University by performing other duties as assigned by the University President. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree from an accredited institution with a record of achievement as a university teacher and scholar. A demonstrated history as an accomplished and experienced leader overseeing a complex academic enterprise, specifically related to academic program planning, and financial and personnel management. Demonstrated success in data-informed decision-making, transparent communication, leading organizational change, and establishing academic priorities that align resources with institutional mission, student success, and long-term sustainability. Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence, effective teaching and learning, and continuous improvement in student success and outcomes. Demonstrated experience supporting institutional and specialized accreditation, academic assessment, and continuous improvement processes. Success in identifying, building, and leveraging external partnerships to yield outcomes aligned with the University’s strategic plan. Qualifications necessary for appointment as a tenured full professor in one of the University’s academic departments. Commitment to collegial, consultative processes and shared governance. Experience at a regional public comprehensive university is a plus. Application Process The Provost Search Committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and continue until the position is filled. The successful candidate is expected to begin work on-site at the University no later than February 2027. To ensure full consideration, application materials should be received by October 13, 2026 , and must include: 1. Letter of interest addressing the required qualifications 2. Current curriculum vitae 3. Names, email addresses, and phone numbers of five professional references, including their relationship to the candidate. Applications and nominations should be submitted in confidence to provostsearch@semo.edu . Additional Information For more information about the search process and the University, please visit https://semo.edu/hr/provost/search-profile-provost . Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5479602/records-specialist-registrars-office": {
      "title": "Records Specialist - Registrar's Office",
      "description": "Records Specialist - Registrar's Office Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600311 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Registrar Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Summary Records Specialist Registrar’s Office Full-Time Primary Responsibilities Research and process outgoing official transcript requests Update student records with grade changes, Credit for Prior Learning (CPL) and exam scores Process permanent record updates (address, name change, citizenship, social security number) Evaluate college transcripts including domestic, military, and international transcripts Collaborate with academic departments regarding transfer equivalencies Build course articulations onto student’s record Maintain data files in Ellucian Banner, Banner Document Management (BDM) and the Transfer Equivalency System (TES) Monitor multiple departmental email accounts Council and provide customer service to students, faculty, staff and the public via phone, email and walk-ins Maintain a comprehensive understanding of the Registrar’s Office and university policies and procedures Provide administrative support as needed to Assistant Registrar for Transfer Articulation Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Knowledge of Microsoft Office Word, Excel and Access Demonstrated ability to learn different and new technologies Experience using email programs Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail Demonstrated ability to handle difficult interactions with diplomacy, tact and in a confidential manner Excellent communication skills (verbal, written, and interpersonal) Work history emphasizes an understanding of customer service and reflects an ability to work with high volume of telephone and customer contacts Demonstrated ability to handle multiple tasks with frequent interruptions Demonstrated ability to synthesize information to make independent decisions with minimal supervision Ability to interact effectively with faculty, staff, students and the public Application Process Application Deadline: To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by September 25, 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Submit the following items by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the job announcement. Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for at a later date, if not submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5405388/student-services-specialist-student-financial-services": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist - Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Student Services Specialist - Student Financial Services Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600215 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Student Financial Services Opening Date 08/19/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Student Services Specialist Student Financial Services Full-Time Student Financial Services is a central student services center that provides end-to-end, student-focused support for financial aid, student accounts, and other university accounts receivable. The Student Service Specialist’s role is to provide counseling to students and other constituents regarding accounts receivable and financial aid, while adhering to University and FERPA policies and ensuring compliance. A major responsibility of the Student Service Specialist is to help students navigate the process of financing their education. Primary Responsibilities Advises and counsels students, parents, agencies, and University staff on all aspects of billing and financial aid programs (federal, state, University, private, military, and other third-party), policies, procedures, practices, office services, and document completion Pre-verifies documents needed for the financial aid verification process Audits students’ accounts to verify the accounts are current and accurate; update records, as needed, to be proactive and resolve problems Advises future, current, and prior students regarding their financial obligations to the University and provides guidance in resolving their balances and setting up payment plans to encourage student retention and customer satisfaction Presents financial literacy information to classes and student organizations that covers all aspects of financing higher education Presents information regarding financial aid and billing practices for parents and students during First Step Orientation Participates in the planning of and training for all SFS staff members regarding customer service and maintenance of customer service level standards Collaborates with faculty and staff to promote cooperative relationships that will result in opportunities to resolve financial concerns and complaints, or other difficult situations Handles all information with tact and discretion and recognizes the confidential and sensitive nature of university business Advocates for a positive student enrollment experience and promotes the University in a positive image Utilizes various University, business, and customer service software programs and assists with system testing and upgrades Assists with the development and implementation of policies and procedures Represents the Student Financial Services Office at outreach events (local high schools, community events, Orientation, etc.) Represents the Student Financial Services Office on various University committees Keeps up to date with university, departmental, federal, and state regulations, policies, and updates Develops and prepares ad hoc reports and assumes other responsibilities as assigned by the Director or Assistant Director Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Experience handling complex customer service issues with the ability to assess situations quickly and react to customers accurately and pleasantly in a timely manner Computer proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel, and demonstrated experience using database query programs Strong critical thinking skills with the ability to solve problems, including the ability to help inexperienced individuals understand policies and processes Ability to handle confidential information, exercise sound judgment, and maintain accurate records and files Experience working as part of a team in a collaborative work environment Excellent communication skills, including writing and editing skills, and the ability to present information to the public as well as in one-on-one meetings Excellent organizational and time-management skills, including the ability to successfully prioritize and manage multiple tasks with minimal supervision Evidence of the ability to analyze, interpret, and implement federal, state, and/or University regulations, policies, and procedures Application Process Application Deadline : Review of applications will begin immediately. To Apply : Submit the following items by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the job announcement: Letter of interest addressing required qualifications Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references will be asked for at a later date if not submitted Additional Information Department Website: Student Financial Services About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts | SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5245055/systems-analyst-programmer-information-technology": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst/Programmer - Information Technology",
      "description": "Systems Analyst/Programmer - Information Technology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600032 Division Finance and Administration Department Information Technology Opening Date 02/20/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Systems Analyst/Programmer Information Technology Full Time Primary Responsibilities Create and maintain application programs supporting the University community; Work with end users to identify and document application requirements and specifications. Design, code, test, maintain, document, and implement computer applications Partner with campus units to implement, configure, and support business applications; Help analyze, troubleshoot, and resolve application issues Develop business reports for functional teams; Work with IT System Administrators to implement roles and access procedures to secure university data Work with third party vendors to integrate software with the University's enterprise systems; Consider data and security needs protecting the assets of the University; Work with IT Data Engineers to implement data synchronization between systems Stay current on program development tools, languages, frameworks, and methods; Research and implement best practices for information and application security Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in computer science or a related field Experience with SQL and developing database queries Experience developing in at least one programming language Ability to effectively analyze and solve complex problems Ability to effectively communicate technical procedures and concepts, both in writing and verbally to individuals without a technical background Experience working in a team environment and ability to work independently with limited supervision Demonstrated experience and understanding of quality customer service * Sponsorship for work authorization is not available for this position. *This position is not fully remote and will require working on-campus in Cape Girardeau, MO. Application Process Application Deadline: The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by March 6 , 2026. To Apply : Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: Letter of interest addressing position qualifications Current Resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for at a later date Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fact Book: Institutional Research Factbook | SEMO SEMO Strategic Action Plan: SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
