      "description": "Temporary Implementer - Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202000661 Division Academic Affairs Department Autism Center Opening Date 06/19/2020 Description Benefits Position Summary Behavior Implementer - Temporary Southeast Missouri State University Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment Temporary part time Positions are available at the Center in Cape Girardeau. Primary Responsibilities: Provide direct care to clients Implement individualized programs for children based on ABA principles Accurately record information on the client’s progress throughout the session Complete daily progress notes Communicate effectively with supervisors, families, and other professionals Abide by all ethical guidelines set forth by the BACB Maintain professionalism with all staff members, clients, families, caregivers, and community organizations Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Willing to complete training to become a Registered Behavior Technician Ability to lift at least 25 pounds, to sit on the floor, and to be physically active with or without accommodations Ability to pass a background check Strong verbal and written communication skills Excellent organizational and time management skills Ability to work with young children Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process To Apply: Send resume and cover letter ( letter should address all required qualifications ) to abruner@semo.edu or call the Autism Center for Diagnosis and Treatment at 573-651-2705. Position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu"
