    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5347829/temporary-piano-accompanist-theatre-and-dance": {
      "title": "Temporary Piano Accompanist - Theatre and Dance",
      "description": "Temporary Piano Accompanist - Theatre and Dance Salary See Position Description Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Temporary Job Number 202600093 Division Academic Affairs Department Theatre and Dance Opening Date 05/19/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Piano Accompanist The Jeanine Larson Dobbins Conservatory of Theatre and Dance Temporary, Part-Time (approximately 444 hours per semester) Up to a 10-month assignment (August-May) with potential for annual renewal Compensation : $35 per hour (with an estimated 444 hours each semester) Primary Responsibilities: Serve as piano accompanist in the areas of Class Voice for Musical Theatre and Musical Theatre Performance as assigned Serve as piano accompanist dance classes as assigned Provide piano accompaniment for mainstage musical rehearsals, as well as assigned conservatory showcases, auditions, BFA reviews, and special presentations Play in pit orchestras as assigned, with the possibility of conducting mainstage musical performances Required Qualifications 3 years’ experience as a professional pianist/accompanist Advanced skills in piano sight reading with ability to play Broadway repertory Ability to play in pit orchestras Willingness to work irregular and flexible hours, including nights and weekends Application Process Application Deadline: The review of applications will begin immediately. The position is available to start on August 10, 2026, and will remain open until filled. To Apply: Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the job announcement: Letter of interest addressing all position requirements Current resume Names, current email addresses, and telephone numbers of three professional references Additional Information The Jeanine Larson Dobbins Conservatory of Theatre and Dance About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching, and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high-quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty, and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts | SEMO Strategic Action Plan Position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
