    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/4214903/workforce-instructor-economic-workforce-development": {
      "title": "Workforce Instructor - Economic & Workforce Development",
      "description": "Workforce Instructor - Economic & Workforce Development Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Temporary Job Number 1 Division President Department Office of Economic and Workforce Development Opening Date 09/21/2023 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Summary Workforce Instructor (Temporary) Division of Economic & Workforce Development Position Summary The Division of Economic & Workforce Development is looking to create a pool of individuals to teach specific classes or programs with a wide variety of experience and subject matter expertise in varying fields, including -- technology, education, leadership, childcare, manufacturing, administrative, and many more. The ideal candidate will have a strong understanding of their subject matter and experience training/teaching in that field. Classes may be offered during the weekday, weekday evenings or weekends depending on the need. These positions are part-time and contracted on a course-by-course basis as needed. This opportunity will allow you to connect with the community and help the workforce gain new skills, improve professional knowledge, and connect with regional resources. Responsibilities: Assist and provide feedback in the creation/execution of training courses in related field Facilitate training sessions and answer questions from participants Evaluate the effectiveness of training programs and make recommendations for improvement Maintain training records and documentation Required Qualifications High school diploma and demonstrated competencies and experience in the discipline/industry of teaching Ability to develop and deliver training programs Excellent communication skills Must be professional and be able to present well in front of others Ability to work independently with minimal supervision Application Process Application Deadline: The review of applications is on-going. To Apply: Submit the following items online by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page: letter of interest addressing all position required qualifications current resume names and contact information of three professional references Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fact Book: Institutional Research Factbook | SEMO SEMO Strategic Action Plan: Strategic Action Plan (semo.edu) Position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5519190/access-services-evening-supervisor-kent-library": {
      "title": "Access Services Evening Supervisor - Kent Library",
      "description": "Access Services Evening Supervisor - Kent Library Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600349 Division Academic Affairs Department Kent Library Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Access Services Evening Supervisor Kent Library Full-Time, full benefits 10-Month Professional Position Working August - May, Sunday: 1:00pm – 9:00 p.m. and Monday – Thursday: 2 p.m. - 11:00pm (off June–July) Note: Work hours differ fall and spring breaks, winter intersession and when there are no classes. Access Services manages Kent Library’s primary user service points. The Access Services evening supervisor provides leadership in establishing and ensuring excellent student, faculty, staff and community guest user services. The evening supervisor is responsible for effective and efficient unit management and operations; including training, supervising and evaluating unit staff. The supervisor is responsible for opening, staffing, and closing the building, and for user and staff safety and security during regular and extended hours. Day-to-day operations include providing courteous, friendly user services; assisting users in finding information and lending/borrowing activities; and organizing and maintaining the Library’s circulating collections. Access Services staff may be required to work during poor weather conditions as Kent Library is an essential university service. Primary Responsibilities Train, supervise and evaluate the Library Assistant IIs and student employees Provide excellent, courteous, friendly user services Ensure the safety and security of library users, resources and spaces Facilitate user access to library services, resources, spaces and resource sharing Provide nighttime reference and research assistance Lead and participate in special projects as requested Manage and maintain Kent Library’s circulating, periodicals and reserve collections Participate in borrowing and lending resource sharing activities Share responsibility for building and facilities coordination Create and maintain digital learning materials; such as library guides Serve on library and university committees Required Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited college or university Minimum two years of work experience in a library; Public services experience a plus Experience providing user services Experience with employee training or supervision Evidence of effective interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills Ability to organize work effectively and handle multiple tasks with frequent interruptions Demonstrated initiative, flexibility and ability to work well as a team member and individually Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, good attention to detail and a high level of accuracy Ability to lead or participate in project planning, implementation and completion Proficiency using computers in a work setting and experience with Microsoft Word and Excel Basic understanding of resource sharing among libraries Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by October 30 , 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You must submit the following for your application materials to be complete. Letter of interest addressing all position qualifications Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Information about Kent Library can be found at: https://library.semo.edu Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5519092/director-of-development-athletics": {
      "title": "Director of Development - Athletics",
      "description": "Director of Development - Athletics Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600237 Division Athletics Department Athletics Opening Date 10/16/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Summary Director of Development for Athletics Full-Time/Term Position Summary Southeast Missouri State University is seeking a motivated, relationship-driven Director of Development to grow philanthropic support for SEMO Athletics and the SEMO Athletics Fund. This position will serve as a frontline fundraiser focused primarily on major gifts, capital project fundraising, leadership annual fund support, and sport-specific fundraising. The position will work closely with Athletics leadership, University Advancement, coaches, athletics staff, and other campus partners to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward donors in support of Redhawk student-athletes and Athletics priorities. Primary Responsibilities Manage a portfolio of Athletics donors and prospects, including identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, stewardship, and ongoing relationship management Develop and execute fundraising strategies to secure major gifts, sport-specific gifts, annual leadership gifts, capital project support, endowment support, and other philanthropic commitments for SEMO Athletics Build and maintain relationships with alumni, former student-athletes, season ticket holders, parents, community leaders, corporate partners, and friends of SEMO Athletics Help grow investment in SEMO Athletics by identifying donor upgrade opportunities, cultivating mid-level donors, supporting donor renewals, and assisting with annual giving strategies as needed Prepare donor proposals, case statements, stewardship reports, impact communications, and other materials that clearly communicate the value and impact of supporting SEMO Athletics Coordinate donor engagement and solicitation strategies in partnership with University Advancement, including prospect management, gift processing, stewardship, database activity, campaign alignment, and reporting Partner with coaches and sport administrators across all SEMO sports to identify fundraising priorities, engage prospects, and support approved sport-specific fundraising initiatives Support the successful operation of fundraising events, home athletic events, emerging revenue generation initiatives, and other external engagement opportunities Use Raiser’s Edge NXT, Paciolan/PacFund, and other platforms to manage prospects, track sales activity, document partner communication, monitor inventory, measure performance, and support revenue forecasting Represent SEMO Athletics at home athletic events, select away athletic events, fundraising events, donor functions, community events, University gatherings, and regional engagement opportunities, including evenings, weekends, and occasional travel as required Ensure all fundraising activity is conducted with professionalism, confidentiality, ethical fundraising practices, and compliance with University policies, Foundation procedures, NCAA rules, conference regulations, and applicable state and federal guidelines Perform other duties as assigned in support of University Advancement and SEMO Athletics priorities Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution Minimum two years of professional experience in fundraising, athletics development, university advancement, alumni relations, nonprofit fundraising, sales, or another relationship-based revenue generation field Demonstrated ability to build relationships, communicate effectively, manage prospects, donors, or customers, and move individuals through a cultivation, solicitation, sales, or stewardship process Demonstrated ability or readiness to identify prospects, conduct outreach, make visits, present opportunities, ask for support, close gifts or revenue commitments, and provide appropriate follow-up and stewardship Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to write professional correspondence, develop proposals or presentation materials, and clearly communicate funding priorities Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, personal initiative, and the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines, relationships, and follow-up activity in a fast-paced environment Ability to work collaboratively with a variety of audiences, including Athletics and University leadership, coaches, staff, donors, alumni, volunteers, community partners, and campus colleagues Ability to use donor databases, CRM systems, or similar technology to manage relationships, track activity, and support data-informed outreach Ability to work frequent evenings and weekends, including home and away athletic events, fundraising events, donor functions, community events, University gatherings, and regional engagement opportunities, with occasional travel as required Commitment to NCAA rules compliance, University policies, donor confidentiality, and ethical standards Possess and maintain a valid driver’s license Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by October 20, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button on the top of the page. You must submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete: • Letter of interest addressing all required position qualifications • Resume • Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
