    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5519227/student-success-manager-enrollment-strategy": {
      "title": "Student Success Manager - Enrollment Strategy",
      "description": "Student Success Manager - Enrollment Strategy Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600355 Division Enrollment Management and Student Success Department Enrollment Management and Student Success Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Student Success Manager Enrollment Strategy Full-Time Southeast Missouri State University seeks a collaborative, service-oriented Student Success Manager to serve as the system administrator for its student success and retention platform. By connecting technology, data, and effective outreach, the Student Success Manager will help the University identify student needs, deliver timely interventions, and support persistence and degree completion. Primary Responsibilities Serve as the system administrator for the University’s student success and retention platform, overseeing configuration, user access, permissions, maintenance, and daily operations Collaborate with advising, academic departments, student support offices, and information technology to develop workflows that support coordinated outreach, early alerts, referrals, and case management Configure and manage student success campaigns, automated communications, tracking items, and follow-up processes to support registration, persistence, and degree completion Develop dashboards and reports to monitor student engagement, re-registration activity, and other student success indicators Partner with information technology and institutional research teams to maintain integrations, troubleshoot issues, and ensure accurate and timely sharing of student data Provide user training, documentation, and ongoing support to promote effective and consistent use of the platform Serve as the primary liaison with the software vendor, coordinating support requests, system updates, and evaluation of new features Maintain procedures for system use and data management that align with university policies, student privacy requirements, and accessibility standards Assess platform effectiveness and recommend enhancements based on user feedback, institutional priorities, and student outcomes Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum three years of relevant experience in higher education, student success, advising, enrollment management, information systems, or a related field Excellent communication and collaboration skills Strong computer and technical skills Proficiency with student information systems for data collection, assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement Demonstrated ability to configure systems or workflows, troubleshoot issues, and translate operational needs into practical technology solutions Detail-oriented with strong organizational and problem-solving abilities Exercises sound judgment Ability to maintain confidentiality when working with sensitive information Demonstrated experience and understanding of person-centered planning and outcomes Commitment to student success Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by October 30, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button on the top of the page. You must submit the following in order for your application materials to be complete: • Letter of interest addressing all required position qualifications • Resume • Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later, if not previously submitted Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential learning with a foundation of liberal arts and sciences, embracing a tradition of access, exceptional teaching and commitment to student success that significantly contributes to the development of the region and beyond. SEMO values access to high quality, affordable education with a broadly representative student body, faculty and staff that respects and celebrates a diverse learning community in a global society. SEMO Fast Facts SEMO Strategic Plan Southeast Missouri State University provides an excellent benefits package. For complete benefit details visit our website at https://semo.edu/hr . Employer Southeast Missouri State University Address 1 University Plaza Cape Girardeau, Missouri, 63701 Phone (573) 651-2206 Website http://www.semo.edu Apply"
