    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5524540/administrative-proctor-testing-services": {
      "title": "Administrative Proctor - Testing Services",
      "description": "Administrative Proctor - Testing Services Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Part-Time Job Number 202600343 Division Academic Affairs Department Testing Services Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Administrative Proctor Testing Services Part-Time The Administrative Proctor will support students and public throughout the testing process. Examples of support include scheduling appointments, admitting test takers, proctoring exams, and data entry. Testing Services provides exams for both students and the public. Excellent customer service is a must. Hours for this position are Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday from 8:00AM-1:00PM. Primary Responsibilities Provides administrative support to the Department. Be able to work in a fast-paced environment with the ability to switch tasks quickly Greet visitors, answer phone lines, schedule appointments, and provide quality customer service to constituencies Calculate, record, balance, and monitor monthly income, expenditures, and account transfers Process purchase requisitions and invoice payments Maintain the departmental calendar Work with faculty and staff from other departments to secure student exams Maintain strict confidentiality regarding exam schedules, exam content, score reports, and student accessibility records Compose and produce letters, memos, and reports Maintain and organize department and student files, both paper and electronic Earn proctor certification credentials for various testing vendors Serve as exam proctor as needed Correspond with current and prospective students Assist students registered with Accessibility Services to create positive testing experiences Supervise and manage student workers; organize the flow of work through the office Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Proficiency in Microsoft Word and Excel, MOS certification is a plus Demonstrated complete administrative skills, including ex