    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/semoedu/promotionaljobs/jobs/5533180/boiler-technician-ii-facilities-management": {
      "title": "Boiler Technician II - Facilities Management",
      "description": "Boiler Technician II - Facilities Management Salary See Position Description Location Cape Girardeau, MO Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202600358 Division Finance and Administration Department Facilities Management Opening Date 10/28/2026 Closing Date 11/11/2026 11:59 PM Central Description Benefits Position Summary BOILER TECHNICIAN II Facilities Management Full Time Starting Wage : $23.15 per hour / $25.26 after successful completion of probationary period Primary Responsibilities Assist Boiler Tech I with urgent needs with equipment failures, malfunctions, etc., and have the ability to stand in for Tech 1 in the event he/she is unavailable for their regularly scheduled shift Maintain and repair boilers and associated equipment in the plant (feed water pumps, valves, regulators, etc.) Assist with the maintenance of the electrical infrastructure and Emergency Power Generator Systems (gen sets, transfer switches, etc.) within the Boiler Plant and campus Maintain and repair condensate pumps and associated system components in all facilities Maintain and repair steam valves, traps, regulators, relief valves, heat exchangers, and all related steam equipment in all facilities Troubleshoot and repair electrical and control systems issues within the plant Repair, replace and/or fabricate piping assemblies (Steel, Copper, PVC, fiber glass) as needed in all systems (steam, chilled, heating, condenser, condensate, etc.) at all facilities by welding, soldering, brazing, etc. Repair, replace and/or install insulation as needed Maintain and repair chemical feed pumps and control systems Perform water tests and adjust chemical feed rates as needed on open and closed systems (steam, chilled, heating, condenser, etc.) Assist in the Preventative Maintenance Program with other plant personnel as directed Perform “Standby” on call duties on a rotating basis with other plant personnel Maintain fountains on the campus to include upkeep and performance of the water systems Assist in the upkeep and appearance of the plant and campus Maintain a valid driver’s license Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Possess a current driver’s license Must live within 30 minutes travel time from the University Experience on steam boiler systems in an educational, commercial or industrial setting Ability to read and work from prints, schematics, and from verbal and written instructions Strong electrical/mechanical ability as evidenced by maintenance experience Ability to operate various pieces of testing equipment (volt/ohm meters, pressure testing instruments, etc.) and skilled in the proper use of hand and power tools Ability to perform shift work on a rotational basis Ability to learn the control systems, electrical systems and switchgears Ability to work and complete assignments with minimal supervision Ability to perform heavy work and lift up to 100 lbs. and to work at heights up to 150 ft. that exist on campus with or without accommodations Ability to work in close or confined spaces for extended periods of time with or without accommodation Willing to participate in training/schooling to continually improve abilities relative to position Demonstrated experience and understanding of customer service Application Process To ensure full consideration, application materials must be received by November 11 , 2026 . The position is available immediately and will remain open until filled. Complete the online application by clicking on the APPLY button at the top of the page. You must submit the following for your application materials to be complete. Letter of interest addressing all position qualifications Current resume Names and contact information of three professional references may be asked for later Additional Information About Southeast Missouri State University (SEMO): Founded in 1873 and accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Southeast Missouri State University provides student-centered education and experiential